\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces South Atlantic Magnetic Anomaly (year 2000; source image from original draft).}}{1}{figure.caption.1}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Day-run mode occupancy and battery energy normalized to the 25 Wh planning reference.}}{27}{figure.caption.88}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Information-bearing functional flow of the planned mission sequence. Windows and guards come from the mission scheduler. The schematic does not assert that every transition is immediate; slew and settling times are accounted for separately.}}{34}{figure.caption.105}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Supervisory decision logic: survival constraints override scheduled science and downlink. Recovery transitions depend on the fault and attitude state; this is a mission-level policy, not an assertion of finalized flight code.}}{35}{figure.caption.108}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Longitudinal concept, not a packaged CAD drawing. Shown gaps and shield thickness are schematic. Dimension sums count active material only. An optional rear detector would lie beyond Block 5 and is not included.}}{39}{figure.caption.111}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Main-block cross-section. Optical isolation between successive X faces is undecided. The front scintillator's coating and SiPM attachment face remain open; this cross-section does not prescribe them.}}{39}{figure.caption.112}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Candidate signal and science-data flow. EJ-550 provides the optical interface. Eleven SiPMs do not specify eleven ADCs. Fast coincidence may occur in analog/ASIC logic while downstream processing is buffered; this architecture remains to be selected.}}{39}{figure.caption.113}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Independent reproduction of the required-$G$ study. Fine intervals require more acceptance for the same counting precision than broad bands; each interval has its own eligible-cell population. This is a count requirement, not an achievable or measured FPDU response.}}{43}{figure.caption.120}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Supplied single thermal history and independent synthetic heat schedule, 1.9--4.9~W. Model predictions; actual case epoch, component mapping and DITL coupling are unverified.}}{52}{figure.caption.131}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Reproduced minima, maxima and weighted means from the same history. The summary's hot/cold names do not establish separate bounding-case runs.}}{52}{figure.caption.132}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces Corrected annual v3 sensitivity, contact-end backlog. Within-contact and pre-contact peaks are given in the tables; this curve is not emitted telemetry.}}{56}{figure.caption.136}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {12}{\ignorespaces Superseded historical source: 24-hour integrated DITL overview: mode timeline, energy and storage, power, pointing, reaction-wheel speed and operational windows.}}{69}{figure.caption.140}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces Corrected 24-hour mode timelines. Display-sampled points do not define the integration weights.}}{74}{figure.caption.143}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14}{\ignorespaces Exposure gates, eligible contact time and native transfer credits for the corrected day runs. Credits are not confirmed ground receipt.}}{75}{figure.caption.144}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {15}{\ignorespaces Startup and Slewing duration from transition logs, shown separately from telemetry occupancy.}}{75}{figure.caption.145}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {16}{\ignorespaces Corrected 365-day exposure, battery envelope and contact availability; epoch 2000-03-01. These are recorded model predictions under unresolved runtime configuration.}}{76}{figure.caption.146}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {17}{\ignorespaces Annual telemetry mode occupancy and cumulative geographic versus acquisition-gate exposure. No mission-success classification is inferred.}}{76}{figure.caption.147}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {18}{\ignorespaces Daily native generation/transfer and maximum source-labelled store. The historical native packet format is not Science Record v3.}}{77}{figure.caption.148}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {19}{\ignorespaces Historical detumble summary. The empirical completion curve retains all 50\,000 rows as denominator; it is not a censor-adjusted survival estimate. Spin-bin proportions do not establish flight initial-condition probabilities.}}{77}{figure.caption.149}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {20}{\ignorespaces Four-month MMSC science-grid output from the supplied simulation archive; model-dependent.}}{79}{figure.caption.151}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {21}{\ignorespaces Twelve-month MSC science-grid output from the supplied simulation archive; model-dependent.}}{80}{figure.caption.152}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {22}{\ignorespaces Extended science-grid classification from the supplied simulation archive; model-dependent.}}{80}{figure.caption.153}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {23}{\ignorespaces Historical modeled SAA proton spectrum. Its title assumes 546 days and $G=0.314$~cm$^2$~sr; these labels do not verify runtime duration or connect it to the new unit-$G$ table. This is not a validated detector measurement.}}{81}{figure.caption.154}%
